.TH LIFELINECTL 8 "2026-11-20" "lifeline 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lifelinectl \- inspect and control the lifeline service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lifelinectl
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lifelinectl
queries, validates, reloads, and overrides the running
.BR lifeline (8)
daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to configuration file (default:
.IR /etc/lifeline/config.toml ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Display the current mode, reason, Ethernet/Wi-Fi interfaces, Wi-Fi health,
external DHCP / peer election state, and active DHCP client leases. Pass
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B validate
Check
.IR config.toml ,
.IR config.env ,
and
.I dhcp_hosts.csv
for syntax or IP/MAC conflicts before starting or reloading.
.TP
.B doctor
Print a diagnostic report covering config validation, binaries, systemd network
services, NetworkManager managed/unmanaged device states, dnsmasq test output,
nftables tables, and recent journal entries.
.TP
.B reload
Hot-reload configuration and the MAC-to-IP table in the running daemon.
.TP
.B force\-mode {primary|secondary|failover|auto}
Force a specific mode for testing or maintenance, or return to
.B auto
control.
.TP
.B prompt [\-\-shell {plain|bash|zsh}] [\-\-color] [\-\-show-stopped]
Print a compact status badge for shell
.B PS1
/
.B PROMPT
integration by reading
.I /run/lifeline/status.json
directly (no root privileges required).
.TP
.B cleanup
Remove runtime firewall rules, policy routes, stale dnsmasq processes, and
temporary NetworkManager profiles. Used automatically by systemd on stop.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check if DHCP is active and which clients hold leases:
.B sudo lifelinectl status
.TP
Validate edited host entries and apply them live:
.B sudo lifelinectl validate && sudo lifelinectl reload
.TP
Force failover mode for testing, then restore automatic mode:
.B sudo lifelinectl force\-mode failover
.br
.B sudo lifelinectl force\-mode auto
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if the daemon is unreachable or a control command
fails, and 2 on invalid configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lifeline/config.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /run/lifeline/control.sock
Control socket used to talk to
.BR lifelined (8).
.SH AUTHOR
Vikram Aggarwal
.SH REPORTING BUGS AND CONTRIBUTING
Bug fixes and feature improvements are warmly encouraged. Include
.B lifelinectl status \-\-json
and
.B journalctl -u lifeline
output when filing issues or submitting patches.
